---
source: crates/tk/tests/scenarios.rs
expression: "p.run(&format!(\"{command} --help\"))"
---
Update the title, body, priority, effort, or parent of a Ticket or Epic

Usage: tk update [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  Display ID or Alias of the Ticket or Epic to update

Options:
  -t, --title <TITLE>        Replace the title with one nonblank line; trim outer spaces and tabs
  -b, --body <BODY>          Replace the body with literal text; an empty value clears it
      --body-file <PATH>     Replace the body from a UTF-8 file, or '-' for stdin; empty input clears it
  -p, --priority <PRIORITY>  Set Priority (P0..P3). Tickets only
      --effort <EFFORT>      Set Effort (low, medium, high). Tickets only
      --no-effort            Clear the Ticket's Effort. Tickets only
  -P, --parent <CONTAINER>   Set the Container, an Epic or a Ticket, by Display ID or Alias. Tickets only
      --no-parent            Remove the Ticket from its current Container. Tickets only
  -h, --help                 Print help
